# Computation and Communication Overlap in Expert Parallel

## Why Overlap Matters in Expert Parallel (EP)

In Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) with Expert Parallel, tokens are routed across GPUs — this requires **All-to-All collective communication** twice per MoE layer:

```
Forward pass:
  All2All_dispatch:   send tokens to expert GPUs    ← communication
  Expert compute:     FFN on local experts          ← computation  
  All2All_combine:    gather results back           ← communication

Backward pass:
  All2All_combine_grad → Expert_grad → All2All_dispatch_grad
```

The naive approach runs these **sequentially**, leaving GPUs idle during communication. The goal: **run computation and communication simultaneously**.

---

## The Core Idea: Chunk-Based Pipeline

Instead of sending ALL tokens at once, split them into **micro-chunks** and pipeline them:

```
Naive (sequential):
  [===All2All_dispatch===][=====Expert FFN=====][===All2All_combine===]
   GPU idle during comm        GPU busy           GPU idle during comm

Overlapped (pipelined):
  Chunk0: [dispatch][FFN][combine]
  Chunk1:      [dispatch][FFN][combine]
  Chunk2:           [dispatch][FFN][combine]
  ...
  Timeline: comm and compute overlap across chunks!
```

---

## Key Mechanism: CUDA Streams

The fundamental building block — different CUDA streams run concurrently:

```python
import torch
import torch.distributed as dist

# Two streams: one for compute, one for communication
compute_stream = torch.cuda.Stream()
comm_stream    = torch.cuda.Stream()

def overlapped_expert_forward(tokens, expert_ffn, num_chunks=4):
    """
    tokens: [num_tokens, hidden_dim]
    Split into chunks, pipeline dispatch → compute → combine
    """
    chunks = tokens.chunk(num_chunks, dim=0)
    results = [None] * num_chunks

    # Pre-allocate receive buffers for all chunks
    recv_buffers = [torch.empty_like(c) for c in chunks]

    for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):
        # ── Communication: dispatch chunk i ──
        with torch.cuda.stream(comm_stream):
            # All2All: send chunk i to expert GPUs
            dist.all_to_all_single(
                recv_buffers[i],   # where to receive
                chunk,             # what to send
                group=ep_group
            )

        # ── Computation: run FFN on chunk i-1 (already received) ──
        if i > 0:
            with torch.cuda.stream(compute_stream):
                # Make compute_stream wait for comm of chunk i-1
                compute_stream.wait_stream(comm_stream)
                results[i-1] = expert_ffn(recv_buffers[i-1])

    # Process last chunk
    with torch.cuda.stream(compute_stream):
        compute_stream.wait_stream(comm_stream)
        results[-1] = expert_ffn(recv_buffers[-1])

    # Synchronize before combine
    torch.cuda.synchronize()

    return torch.cat(results, dim=0)
```

