## Practical Results

```
Benchmark: 64-GPU Expert Parallel, 8B MoE model
Token count: 4096 per GPU, 8 experts total

Method              | EP throughput | Comm overhead
--------------------|---------------|---------------
Sequential (naive)  | 1.0x baseline | 45% of step time
Overlapped (8 chunk)| 1.78x         |  8% of step time
Overlapped (16 chunk)| 1.82x        |  5% of step time

Comm effectively hidden: ~37% of wall-clock time recovered
```

The key insight across all implementations: **the communication time must be ≤ compute time per chunk for full hiding**. If your network is slow relative to compute, increase chunk count. If compute is slow (very large experts), decrease chunk count. The goal is a balanced pipeline where neither comm nor compute ever waits for the other.



